    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 25 Wellington Road is a period terraced residence of approximately 320 sq m (3,498 sq\nft), dating from the 1870s and standing on a site of some 496 sq m on one of Dublin 4's most\ncelebrated roads. A protected structure (RPS No. 8401), the house retains its original\nproportions and detailing — ornate ceiling covings, centre roses, marble chimneypieces and recessed sash windows — alongside a substantial three-storey rear extension completed in 2007/08, when the property was renovated throughout and both gardens professionally landscaped.\n\nThe accommodation is arranged as two storeys over garden level. At hall level, a pair of\ninterconnecting reception rooms forms the architectural heart of the house, each with a\nKilkenny marble fireplace, corniced ceiling and centre rose, linked by double doors and\nrunning the full depth of the original building. The garden level holds the informal family\naccommodation, culminating in a large kitchen and breakfast room where four sets of glazed\ndoors open to the terrace and the west-facing walled rear garden. In all there are four double\nbedrooms, three of them en suite, a principal bathroom on the second-floor return and a\nstudy with fitted bookcases and a box-bay window seat on the garden-level return.\n\nTo the front, a landscaped garden of gravel paths and box hedging is set behind wrought-iron railings, with off-street parking for two cars behind electric gates — a rare advantage on\nWellington Road. The house was repainted inside and out in 2025/26, with new carpets\nfitted to the principal rooms, bedrooms and staircase, and is offered in walk-in condition.\n\nWellington Road is a wide, tree-lined road of predominantly period terraces on the west side\nof Ballsbridge, close to the junction with Elgin Road. Baggot Street is within 450 m,\nBallsbridge and Donnybrook villages within 650 m and 800 m, and Herbert Park within a\nten-minute walk; St Stephen's Green lies 1.2 km away. The RDS, the Aviva Stadium and\nFitzwilliam Lawn Tennis Club are close at hand, and the road is well placed for a number of\nDublin's leading junior and senior schools."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHall Level - \n\n\nEntrance Hall - 10.15m x 1.95m\nTiled floor, corniced ceiling and centre rose, with a feature archway framing the stairs.\n\nDrawing Room - 4.95m x 4.95m\nFront-facing reception room with a Kilkenny marble fireplace and open fire, corniced ceilingand centre rose. Double doors open to the dining room, allowing the two rooms to be used asone.\n\nDining Room - 5.10m x 4.95m\nRear-facing and matching the drawing room in scale, with a second Kilkenny marblefireplace and open fire, corniced ceiling and centre rose.\n\nGarden-Level Return - \n\n\nStudy - 4.70m x 3.00m\nFitted bookcases and a timber box-bay window with window seat, overlooking the reargarden.\n\nGarden Level - \n\n\nHallway - 12.13m x 1.95m\nUnderstairs and under-step storage, with independent access to the front garden.\n\nSitting Room - 2.70m x 4.95m\nFamily room with an open fireplace, built-in shelving and double doors opening directly tothe rear patio.\n\nKitchen/ Breakfast Room - 9.20m x 3.90m\nA full-width kitchen and dining space along the rear of the house, fitted with an extensiverange of cabinetry around a large central island. The specification includes an Aga range, afive-ring gas hob, double ovens, two integrated dishwashers, an undercounter Belfast sinkand a pull-out larder. Four sets of glazed doors open to the patio and the west-facing gardenbeyond.\n\nUtility Room - 1.85m x 3.70m\nFitted wall and floor units, Belfast sink, plumbed for washing machine and dryer; separateboiler room.\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.35m x 4.95m\nDouble bedroom with terrazzo floor and a cast-iron fireplace, served by an en suite showerroom with walk-in shower and heated towel rail.\n\nGuest WC - 1.40m x 1.95m\nTiled floor, WC and wash-hand basin.\n\nFirst-Floor Return - \n\n\nBedroom 3 - 5.10m max x 3.10m\nDouble bedroom with built-in wardrobes and a Juliet balcony to the rear.\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nLanding - 7.55m x 2.00m\nFeature archway and roof light, bringing natural light to the upper floor.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.50m x 7.00m\nPrincipal bedroom to the front, with wainscot panelling concealing a full run of built-inwardrobes. The en suite shower room has twin wash-hand basins, a walk-in shower, a Veluxwindow, heated towel rail and fitted storage.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.39m x 4.90m\nRear-facing double bedroom with built-in wardrobes and an en suite shower room withwalk-in shower, heated towel rail and mirrored cabinet.\n\nSecond-Floor Return - \n\n\nBathroom - 3.65m x 2.25m\nPrincipal bathroom with a freestanding roll-top bath, WC, wash-hand basin and bidet,finished with wall panelling and a timber floor.\n\nOutside - \nThe front garden is laid in gravel with box-hedged beds behind wrought-iron railings, withvehicular electric gates and parking for two cars. To the rear, a paved terrace off the kitchensteps up to the west-facing walled garden, landscaped and bordered by mature trees.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Period terraced residence of approximately 320 sq m / 3,498 sq ft</li><li> Protected structure, RPS No. 8401; BER exempt</li><li> Three-storey rear extension and full renovation, 2007/08</li><li> Repainted internally and externally in 2025/26; new carpets throughout the principal rooms</li><li> Four double bedrooms, three en suite; principal bathroom with roll-top bath</li><li> Interconnecting drawing and dining rooms with Kilkenny marble fireplaces</li><li> West-facing walled rear garden; landscaped gardens front and rear</li><li> Off-street parking for two cars behind electric wrought-iron gates</li><li> Underfloor heating at garden level; gas-fired central heating</li><li> Freehold</ul>"
      },
